#lang saffron
;; docs/guides/saffron-guide.md, "Refinements become runtime contracts": a
;; violation the compiler CANNOT see panics `Contract violated`.
;;
;; The distinction the guide draws is the point of this fixture. Written with a
;; literal -- `(pos -3)` -- the compiler PROVES the violation and reports
;; TUR-E0371 "cannot be proved statically", which is a different claim
;; entirely. `hide` launders the value through an unannotated parameter so the
;; check is the runtime one the guide describes.
;;
;; The first draft of the guide got this wrong and would have told readers a
;; static error was a runtime panic. Found by running the example.
;;
;; "before" is printed first so this distinguishes "panicked at the contract"
;; from "never ran".

(defn pos [n : #refine{v : any | (> v 0)}] n)
(defn hide [x] x)

(defn main []
  (println "before")
  (println (cast (pos (hide -3)) int))
  0)
